## 12. Commercial Evaluation

Use by or on behalf of a for-profit entity for procurement, product evaluation, investor diligence, acquisition diligence, customer demonstration, commercial feasibility analysis, or internal product-development decisions constitutes Commercial Use.

Such evaluation requires separate written permission.

This provision does not prohibit an individual researcher employed by a commercial entity from conducting genuinely personal or academic Research Use independently of that entity’s commercial purposes.

