## 16. Security Research

Good-faith security research is permitted where it is conducted to identify, reproduce, document, or remediate vulnerabilities in the Licensed Materials.

Security research must not intentionally cause unnecessary harm, unauthorized access to third-party systems, data exfiltration, service disruption, or Offensive Use.

Responsible disclosure is encouraged.

