## 25. Compliance Records

Individual researchers conducting ordinary personal or academic Research Use are not required to maintain formal compliance records.

Organizations exercising rights under this license must maintain reasonable records sufficient to demonstrate compliance with restrictions concerning Commercial Use, Production Use, Hosted Services, AI/ML Development Use, and Model Extraction.

Upon reasonable written request relating to suspected material breach, an organizational Licensee must provide a reasonable written description of its relevant use.

---

## 26. Termination

Rights under this license terminate upon material breach.

Except for the breaches identified in Section 27, the Licensee shall have thirty (30) days after receiving written notice of breach to cure the breach where cure is reasonably possible.

If cured within that period, rights under this license are automatically reinstated.

---

## 27. Immediate-Termination Breaches

The following intentional activities may result in immediate termination without a cure period:

27.1 unauthorized Commercial Use;

27.2 unauthorized Production Use;

27.3 unauthorized Hosted Service operation;

27.4 intentional AI/ML Development Use;

27.5 intentional Model Extraction;

27.6 intentional Offensive Use;

27.7 deliberate removal of licensing or copyright notices for the purpose of unauthorized exploitation.

Termination does not extinguish accrued claims arising from prior breach.

---

## 28. Effect of Termination

Upon termination, You must cease unauthorized use of the Licensed Materials.

Where prohibited Model Artifacts or unauthorized commercial derivatives were created in breach, You must cease using and distributing them and, where legally and technically practicable, delete copies under Your control.

Obligations that by their nature survive termination shall survive.

